findings.body:
The updated `EmbeddingServerAppInsideIframe_WithCompressionEnabled_Fails` assertion uses `&&`. A single browser log entry can only be the old `Refused to frame` message or the new `Framing ... violates` message, never both, so `ParseErrorMessageRegexOld.IsMatch(...) && ParseErrorMessageRegexNew.IsMatch(...)` is always false. The message text also says "match one of the CSP error patterns", which contradicts the code.

::diff{file="src/Components/test/E2ETest/ServerExecutionTests/WebSocketCompressionTests.cs" lines="106-110"}

::callout{type="warning"}
This is a fail-always assertion in an E2E test, so it either blocks the release-branch pipeline or gets quarantined without anyone noticing the real cause. Fix it by using `||`, which matches the stated intent of accepting either the old or new browser wording.

::suggestion{file="src/Components/test/E2ETest/ServerExecutionTests/WebSocketCompressionTests.cs" lines="106-110"}
Assert.True(
    ParseErrorMessageRegexOld.IsMatch(logs[0].Message) ||
    ParseErrorMessageRegexNew.IsMatch(logs[0].Message),
    $"Expected log message to match one of the CSP error patterns: {ParseErrorMessageRegexOld} or {ParseErrorMessageRegexNew}. Actual: {logs[0].Message}");

For internal builds, the source-build step now points the runtime source feed at `https://ci.dot.net/internal` instead of `https://dotnetbuilds.blob.core.windows.net/internal`. The read token `dotnetbuilds-internal-container-read-token-base64` is passed with the URL, so the host and the token's scope both matter. Nothing in this PR confirms that the new host serves the same internal runtime feed, or that the token is valid there. If it isn't, source-build fails for internal builds. If it is, the token is now sent to a different origin.

::diff{file="eng/common/core-templates/steps/source-build.yml" lines="44-44"}

::callout{type="security"}
This is an arcade-synced change, so the author probably isn't the right person to decide it. Still, the reviewer should confirm with the arcade owners that `ci.dot.net/internal` is the intended endpoint and accepts this token. The PR description doesn't mention the change.

The default `condition` for the source-index stage changes from empty (always run) to `eq(variables['Build.SourceBranch'], 'refs/heads/main')`. Release and PR builds will now skip source indexing. That may well be intended arcade behavior, but it's a pipeline behavior change in an automated sync that the description doesn't call out.

::diff{file="eng/common/core-templates/job/source-index-stage1.yml" lines="9-9"}

The file is arcade-owned, so the fix belongs upstream. For this PR, the reviewer should confirm that skipping source indexing on non-main branches is intended for the release/9.0 branch.

`ReceiveAsync` now installs the next `_receiveTcs` before the zero-byte check and before `CopyTo`. The zero-byte fix is a real improvement: previously a zero-byte read returned early without resetting the TCS, so the already-completed task was returned again on the next call. The ordering change has a side effect, though. If `res.Item2.CopyTo(buffer)` throws because the buffer is too small, the message has already been consumed from the TCS and cannot be re-read. The old code would have left the completed TCS in place. The test double doesn't exercise this path, so it's low risk.

::diff{file="src/SignalR/server/StackExchangeRedis/test/RedisEndToEnd.cs" lines="409-416"}

A short comment on why the reset happens first would help future readers.
